  "description": "**Authoritative current list.** Promoted from `DECK-V2.md` on 2026-09-08 after the damage pass\nproved out; the previous V1 list is retired to `versions/2026-09-08-v1-retired.md` and the\nSideboard: `SIDEBOARD.md`.\n\n**The chain build (`DECK-V3.md`) sits beside this file**, built 2026-09-08 after an opponent\nended a game on turn 5 with the same commander. Both are Bracket 3 at 3/3 Game Changers; this\none grinds damage across turns 4–7, that one aims for one doubling turn. Test both — the\nmechanism is in `research/turn-5-chain-2026-09-08.md`.\n\n**What this list is:** three slots sit in *spell → damage conversion* (Guttersnipe, Fated\nFirepower, Nico Minoru), one one-shot mana slot is burn (Boltwave), the tenth win condition is\na tutor (Gamble), and Ancient Tomb is a Mountain to keep Game Changers at 3/3. Converters\n5 → 8: a converter in the first 12 cards goes from ~48% to ~66% of games.\n\n**Gameplan:** turns 3–5 put a *converter* down before a mana engine; turns 4–7 cast your spells\n(each one now deals 4–12 to each opponent) and bank the rituals under Electro / Ashling; the\nX-spell is the closer, not the plan. Blackblade on Wanda by turn 5 when drawn. With creature\npingers out, take Fiery Confluence's \"2 to each opponent\" mode three times — the creature mode\nis the one that kills your own board.\n\n**Sequencing note:** on a Neheb turn, burn in your *precombat* main, then collect {R} per point\nof life your opponents lost at the start of your *postcombat* main and cast the X-spell there.\nThe postcombat main phase happens whether or not you attack (rule 500.1).",
